					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-154062#post-2766187</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-154062/scp-764#post-2766187</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 13 Mar 2017 06:23:12 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>CCKinnison</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1185977</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I like the SCP, and the log is great&#8230;<br /> The containment procedures&#8230; ugh.</p> <p>2 &quot;Class 1&quot; Researchers? And no one present unless a Level 4 is overseeing&#8230; or a destruction attempt?</p> <p>1: SCP doesn't DO destruction attempts any more&#8230; generally. And if they did, they'd be overseen carefully.</p> <p>2: &quot;Class 1&quot; - no such animal.<br /> <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/security-clearance-levels">http://www.scp-wiki.net/security-clearance-levels</a><br /> I might buy 2 Level 3 Researchers, with a 4 watching, but that's quite a bit of research power.</p> <p>Actually, the whole sentence about the unlocking mechanisms&#8230; are the mechanisms inside the hazard chamber (one assumes)? Where are the CONTROLS for the locks? (presumably outside the chamber, and THAT'S what needs 2 people working to unlock)<br /> Wearing the locking gauntlets seems to render it impossible to experiment with the puppets. If that's the goal, there should be a simple, explicit prohibition against such &quot;further&quot; experimentation. The gauntlets can be then described as something used to move the container holding the Scip.</p> <p>Also, what about waldos?</p> <hr /> <p>Basically, like the Scip. Do NOT like the containment section/research protocols. No vote.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
